  Slug: panache
  DisplayName: Panache
  IconPath: icons/commodities/treasure/crown-gold-laurel-wreath.webp
  Description: 'You care as much about the way you accomplish something as whether
    you actually accomplish it in the first place. When you perform an action with
    particular style, you can leverage this moment of verve to perform spectacular,
    deadly maneuvers. This heightened state of flair is called panache. @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect:
    Panache] You gain panache by performing actions that have the bravado trait.
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Tumble Through] and additional actions
    determined by your swashbuckler''s style gain the bravado trait when you use
    them. The GM might determine that a check to perform a particularly daring action,
    such as swinging on a chandelier or sliding down a drapery, can gain the bravado
    trait. These checks typically involve at least a single action and a non-trivial
    DC. Normally, you gain and use panache only in combat encounters; when an encounter
    ends, you lose panache. Powerful finisher actions, including @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Confident
    Finisher], can be used only while you have panache and cause you to lose your
    panache.'
